{"id": "EUVD-2026-108924", "enisaUuid": "76e595a4-61e5-3c02-95b3-72e732ebb2f5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nflow_dissector: avoid u16 truncation of hlen in bpf_flow_dissect()\n\nbpf_flow_dissect() sanitizes the offsets returned by the BPF program\nwith clamp_t(u16, ..., hlen).\n\nIf hlen is bigger than 65535, the upper bound is truncated before\nthe comparison. For instance, with hlen == 65536, both nhoff and\nthoff are forced to zero, even if the program returned sane values.\n\nThis is the same class of bug as the one fixed in commit 99bda1ecbd56\n(\"flow_dissector: avoid u16 truncation of skb->len when computing\nthoff\"). That fix does not cover the BPF path, because\n__skb_flow_dissect() returns early when a BPF flow dissector\nhandles the packet.\n\nstruct bpf_flow_keys stores nhoff and thoff as u16, so cap hlen\nto U16_MAX before clamping.\n\nFound by sashiko while reviewing the commit above.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:19:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:19:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c44c02c930c6583b235a1937c69ff716c4bb4514", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3fb5ad2951a6df92c98f4f06cd70f20c50a2eb2a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc18eb0e9941162c03f03f411ed7f6c339d91fa0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/61b43a51a55929ec040bee3ea51af2121b956d05", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f202578efc738b883cfa04889eb97328914265a7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98950"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "23df5ed0-ffff-3eaf-a09d-61f82ffc17dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "2aee7fb7-40c5-31af-b3fd-bce77a257b2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "48be36d0-0151-3ccc-af6c-1917367612e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d58e468b1112dcd1d5193c0a89ff9f98b5a3e8b9 <f202578efc738b883cfa04889eb97328914265a7"}, {"id": "5255b06d-f5f4-38bf-95e6-2029cab3051e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "559b37d1-5b93-3ca0-8862-f5875e7cb144", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d58e468b1112dcd1d5193c0a89ff9f98b5a3e8b9 <3fb5ad2951a6df92c98f4f06cd70f20c50a2eb2a"}, {"id": "66177ae4-c137-34ab-8610-dfe8c1993a95", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.20"}, {"id": "8f63f512-30c6-36a7-984c-31caa7d9c203", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d58e468b1112dcd1d5193c0a89ff9f98b5a3e8b9 <c44c02c930c6583b235a1937c69ff716c4bb4514"}, {"id": "a64caa6b-8d22-323b-846a-23a1a9be89ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "ba815cc6-cb20-34b0-8074-7002a5f66a76", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "c678b95d-dde2-3f22-acbc-47b8bc83fb63", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d58e468b1112dcd1d5193c0a89ff9f98b5a3e8b9 <61b43a51a55929ec040bee3ea51af2121b956d05"}, {"id": "e2f513a8-b523-3235-a158-d58b9bbd3c27", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d58e468b1112dcd1d5193c0a89ff9f98b5a3e8b9 <cc18eb0e9941162c03f03f411ed7f6c339d91fa0"}, {"id": "ea6af3d7-5889-3225-9c12-52208f65938d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "faf45795-86a1-3d6f-9e2a-681fa1981b5d", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}